    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d681">

                <pb facs="0802" n="784" sameAs="frus:frus1946v11/pg784"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">837.61351/6–2546</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Chargé in Cuba</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Woodward</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">restricted</hi>
                        <lb/> No. 826</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-06-25">June 25, 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Acting Secretary of State encloses for transmittal to Mr. Evaristo Sotolongo,
                    Acting President of the Cuban Sugar Stabilization Institute, a letter dated June
                    25, 1946, together with a <hi rendition="#italic">modus vivendi</hi><anchor
                        n="43" xml:id="d681-f1"/> for the purchase of the 1946 sugar crop, from Mr.
                    James H. Marshall, Director, Sugar Branch, Production and Marketing
                    Administration, United States Department of Agriculture. There are also enclosed
                    copies of these documents for the Embassy’s files.</p>



                <xi:include href="d681-a1.xml" xpointer="d681-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
